DESCRIPTION >
    Phase 4d (Pattern C row-pull). Pageviews for a SPECIFIC set of converted
    visitors over the lookback window, replacing HogQL's IN-list-filtered pvSql
    in getAiPlatformAttributionLive (api/lib/attribution-engine.js:471-503).
    Feeds the SAME unchanged selectAiTouchForConversion (engine:310-347) and
    detectAiPlatformFromEvent (channel-classifier.js:103-134) — both confirmed
    by reading the code to be single-row JS selection (no per-column argMax,
    no fusion-across-rows risk the way Pattern A's last_touch had; see
    tinybird/PHASE4_4D_PLAN.md §1). This pipe's job is row-pull parity only.

    CHUNKING KEPT, not removed (tinybird/PHASE4_4D_PLAN.md §2.3 / 4d report):
    Tinybird's documented SQL-length limit is 128KB
    (https://www.tinybird.co/docs/forward/pricing/limits). {{Array(...)}}
    interpolates into the final SQL text, so a large visitor_id array inflates
    the query toward that ceiling — measured ~91KB for 2000 realistic-length
    UUIDs from the array alone. The caller MUST chunk visitor_ids at 100 per
    call (mirroring api/lib/attribution-engine.js's existing
    AI_ATTRIBUTION_VISITOR_BATCH_SIZE=100 / chunkVisitorIds), looping this pipe
    once per chunk — NOT pass an unbounded array in one call.

    IDENTITY FIX (rule #19c): this pipe's IN-list filter was `visitor_id IN`,
    but live HogQL builds the IN-list from `c.distinct_id`
    (attribution-engine.js:454) and filters with `distinct_id IN (...)`
    (attribution-engine.js:501) — resolved here from "flagged, not decided"
    to "distinct_id, matching live HogQL exactly." Changed the WHERE-clause
    filter and the ORDER BY's leading key from visitor_id to distinct_id.
    Under single-identity (distinct_id == visitor_id, the only case any
    producer or fixture currently exercises) this is numerically a no-op, but
    the pipe's structural filter key now matches the live query.

    SCOPE LIMIT (re-validated, post-fix, only for distinct_id == visitor_id):
    a merged identity (server-events.js's user_id path) could diverge
    visitor_id from distinct_id (normalize.js:251-253) — deferred to the
    $identify / identity-reconciliation backlog item, same as 4c. Merged-
    identity case remains UNVERIFIED — no fixture exercises it.

    NOT YET PUSHED (no `tb push`/`tb deploy` run — validated via read-only
    `tb --cloud sql` only, per standing no-push rule).

    PHASE 6 ADDITION (N+1 rewrite, aiplatform:505): added optional
    page_size/page_offset params, preserving the SAME pagination/continuation
    safety the old JS loop already had (LIMIT AI_ATTRIBUTION_PAGEVIEW_PAGE_SIZE
    OFFSET offset, stopping when a page returns fewer rows than page_size) —
    NOT deleting the bound, per the dispatch's explicit caveat. Default
    page_size (5000) matches the old AI_ATTRIBUTION_PAGEVIEW_PAGE_SIZE
    exactly, so behavior is unchanged for any caller that omits these params.

TOKEN "phase4_pageviews_by_visitors_read" READ

NODE pageviews_by_visitors_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        visitor_id,
        distinct_id,
        timestamp,
        utm_source,
        utm_medium,
        utm_campaign,
        referrer,
        ai_source,
        gclid,
        gbraid,
        wbraid,
        fbclid,
        msclkid,
        ttclid,
        li_fat_id,
        li_fatid,
        twclid,
        dclid,
        snapclid,
        pclid,
        sccid,
        ko_click_id,
        page_url,
        utm_term
    FROM events_by_visitor
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$pageview'
      AND distinct_id IN {{ Array(visitor_ids, 'String', required=True) }}
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(lookback_from, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
    ORDER BY distinct_id, timestamp ASC
    LIMIT {{ Int32(page_size, 5000) }}
    OFFSET {{ Int32(page_offset, 0) }}

TYPE endpoint
